{
  "summary": "This study engineered hypoxia-tolerant supramolecular nanomicelles (TBBP NPs) to enhance NIR-II phototheranostics. The approach combined molecular conformation engineering with supramolecular assembly, enabling efficient photothermal conversion, Type I photodynamic therapy, and immunogenic pyroptosis under hypoxia. In 4T1 tumors, TBBP NPs achieved 92% primary tumor inhibition and 47.7% distant tumor inhibition via synergistic imaging, phototherapy, and immune activation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TBBP NPs exhibit 42.17% photothermal conversion efficiency and broadband NIR-II emission (1000-1600 nm)",
    "TBBP NPs induce caspase-3/GSDME-mediated immunogenic pyroptosis, promoting dendritic cell maturation and CD8+ T cell infiltration",
    "In 4T1 tumors, TBBP NPs achieved 92.0% primary tumor inhibition and 47.7% distant tumor inhibition through synergistic Type I PDT and photothermal therapy"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo tumor model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular conformation engineering strategy for hypoxia-tolerant phototheranostic nanocarriers that synergistically integrate imaging, phototherapy, and immunotherapy, providing a generalizable design principle for multifunctional cancer theranostics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates programming hemostasis and healing through charge-density modulation in thermo-responsive hydrogels. By tuning ε-polylysine cationic density to create EPL-C2, the researchers developed a fibrinogen-selective hydrogel (FN-C2) that enhances hemostasis without excessive coagulation activation. FN-C2 also enabled sustained insulin delivery, accelerating wound healing via improved granulation tissue and collagen deposition.",
  "key_findings": [
    "EPL-C2 selectively interacts with fibrinogen over plasma proteins",
    "FN-C2 hydrogel enhances hemostasis without broad coagulation cascade activation",
    "FN-C2 with insulin delivery accelerates skin and intestinal wound healing"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a universal design strategy for programmable hemostatic interfaces that inherently support integrated therapeutic delivery, advancing wound dressing technology through charge-density optimization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates perforin's role in anti-tumor immunity by revealing a Gzm-independent mechanism where perforin induces ferroptosis in tumor cells. Perforin forms pores that increase iron uptake via transferrin receptor endocytosis, leading to mitochondrial iron accumulation, dysfunction, and ferroptosis. Dietary iron supplementation reduced tumor growth in mice, and higher perforin expression correlated with better patient survival and immune checkpoint response.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Perforin directly triggers ferroptosis in tumor cells without granzymes",
    "Perforin increases cellular iron uptake by promoting transferrin receptor endocytosis",
    "Higher perforin expression correlates with improved patient survival and immune checkpoint response"
  ],
  "study_type": "Murine tumor models and human patient data",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes perforin as a direct executor of ferroptosis in cancer cell death, providing a novel mechanism for perforin's role in anti-tumor immunity beyond granzyme-dependent pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates using rare-earth oxide clusters to modulate electronic structures of zinc single-atom sites for enhanced oxygen reduction reaction (ORR) catalysis. By engineering LaOx clusters proximal to Zn sites on porous carbon, the catalyst achieves a high half-wave potential of 0.90 V and stable performance in alkaline media. It demonstrates superior ORR activity in non-precious-metal electrocatalysts with a zinc-air battery power density of 177.3 mW cm-2.",
  "key_findings": [
    "LaOx clusters remotely modulate Zn site electronic structures to enhance ORR activity",
    "Catalyst achieves 0.90 V half-wave potential and 177.3 mW cm-2 power density in zinc-air batteries",
    "Theoretical calculations confirm improved electron transfer efficiency via strengthened Zn site interactions"
  ],
  "study_type": "Electrocatalysis study with single-atom catalysts",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a strategy for long-range electronic modulation of single-atom sites using rare-earth clusters, advancing understanding of how to engineer electrocatalytic activity through hierarchical electronic interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered hybrid nanovesicles (SS-hNVs) by fusing membranes from senescent cancer cells and senescence-mimetic red blood cells to create artificial antigen-presenting cells (aAPCs) that integrate endogenous tumor antigen display with spleen-directed biodistribution. SS-aAPCs provided coordinated TCR, costimulatory, and cytokine signals, expanding antigen-specific CD8+ T cells and enhancing tumor suppression in mouse models, with PD-L1 blockade improving outcomes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SS-hNVs combine endogenous tumor antigen display from senescent cancer cells with spleen-targeted biodistribution from senescence-mimetic red blood cells",
    "SS-aAPCs expanded antigen-specific CD8+ T cells and TCF-1+PD-1+ progenitor-like populations in tumor models",
    "Combination with PD-L1 blockade enhanced tumor control in B16-OVA and MC38 mouse models"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo mouse models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a modular biomaterial strategy for systemically administered aAPCs that coordinate molecular immune signaling with organ-level biodistribution, enabling endogenous antigen-specific T-cell priming without genetic modification."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluates in vivo genome editing using AAV9 vectors for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD) therapy in preclinical models and early human trials. It demonstrated targeted dystrophin restoration in mice and primates with no dose-limiting toxicity, but a fatal adverse event occurred in one participant at the highest dose due to complement activation and cytokine release. The findings highlight immunologic risks and the narrow therapeutic window for AAV-CRISPR therapies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Targeted genome editing restored partial dystrophin in humanized DMD mice",
    "Efficient on-target editing with no dose-limiting toxicity in non-human primates",
    "One participant experienced fatal adverse event at high dose due to complement activation and cytokine response"
  ],
  "study_type": "Open-label, dose-escalation clinical trial with preclinical models",
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides initial human proof-of-concept for muscle genome editing while emphasizing the critical immunologic risks and narrow therapeutic window of systemic AAV-CRISPR therapies, necessitating safer dosing strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines bio-integrated edge computing systems for smart health applications, analyzing computing architectures, sensing strategies, and energy solutions to enable continuous, autonomous healthcare monitoring and intervention. It identifies key approaches for on-device data processing, signal fidelity enhancement, and energy efficiency to support scalable, adaptive healthcare systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Analysis of computing architectures including von Neumann and emerging paradigms like compute-in-memory and neuromorphic systems",
    "Discussion of sensing strategies to improve signal fidelity and efficient information representation at biointerfaces",
    "Review of energy solutions enabling continuous, autonomous operation of bio-integrated systems"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational framework for integrating computing, sensing, and energy strategies in bio-integrated edge systems, advancing the development of autonomous, scalable healthcare monitoring and intervention platforms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the use of an on-demand biocatalytic dual oxygen spray to target hypoxia-ferroptosis in chronic wounds. The spray, composed of silk fibroin, aloe vera mucilage, and hemoglobin, releases oxygen upon application to alleviate hypoxia and restore redox balance. It suppressed lipid peroxidation, limited iron overload, and enhanced antioxidant defenses, accelerating healing in ischemic and diabetic wounds in preclinical models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SAH-Hp spray triggers peroxide-responsive O2 release via hemoglobin biocatalysis",
    "Sustained oxygenation suppresses lipid peroxidation and iron overload",
    "Accelerated healing in ischemic and diabetic wounds with reduced hypoxic stress"
  ],
  "study_type": "Preclinical validation in rabbit ear ischemic wounds and streptozotocin-induced diabetic wounds",
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes a targeted oxygenation strategy to disrupt hypoxia-driven ferroptosis, offering a clinically translatable approach for managing chronic hypoxic wounds through restoration of redox and iron homeostasis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used deep whole-genome sequencing of 3,36:7 maize inbred lines to investigate rare variants' contributions to agronomic traits. It identified 411 independent association signals for 10 traits, with 359 linked to globally rare variants. Rare variants exhibited effect sizes 2.4 times larger than common variants and captured significant phenotypic variance in traits under adaptive selection, particularly in temperate maize.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Deep sequencing of 3,367 maize inbred lines revealed 75.3 million variants, 79.2% of which were rare",
    "411 independent association signals for 10 agronomic traits, 359 attributable to globally rare variants",
    "Rare variants showed effect sizes 2.4 times those of common variants and captured substantial phenotypic variance in traits under adaptive selection"
  ],
  "study_type": "Deep whole-genome sequencing of diverse maize inbred lines",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that rare variants play a significant role in the genetic architecture of complex agronomic traits in maize, providing critical resources for functional studies and breeding programs."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing ionic conductivity and deformability in inorganic solid electrolytes for all-solid-state batteries. By applying cyclic nonequilibrium thermal processing to Li3InCl6, the researchers optimized particle size, induced local amorphization, and created Li vacancies. This approach increased ionic conductivity from 1.3 to 6.8 mS/cm and reduced Young's modulus from 42.3 to 17.6 GPa, enabling stable battery operation at 2 MPa.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cyclic nonequilibrium thermal processing of Li3InCl6 improved ionic conductivity from 1.3 to 6.8 mS/cm",
    "Reduction in Young's modulus from 42.3 to 17.6 GPa enhanced compressibility",
    "Optimized solid electrolyte enabled stable cycling at low pressure (2 MPa) with high areal capacity (7.7 mAh/cm²)"
  ],
  "study_type": "Cyclic nonequilibrium thermal processing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a structural engineering strategy to overcome mechanical and ionic transport barriers in solid electrolytes, providing a pathway to practical low-pressure all-solid-state batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This review integrates vascular normalization biology with vascularized tumor-on-chip models to explore tumor vasculature dynamics. It examines how tumor microenvironment features influence vascular function and therapeutic responses, highlighting challenges in clinical translation and the potential of on-chip platforms for studying normalization windows and treatment optimization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Vascular normalization transiently improves perfusion and drug delivery by restoring vessel structure",
    "Tumor-on-chip models can quantify microenvironment features like extracellular matrix remodeling and hemodynamics",
    "Clinical translation faces hurdles including transient normalization windows and adaptive resistance mechanisms"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work bridges fundamental vascular normalization mechanisms with engineered tumor models, providing a framework for mechanistic studies of vascular therapy responses and precision oncology applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether symbionts in animal-microbe symbioses remain immobile after losing motile appendages. Using long-term tracking, fluorescence, and electron microscopy, researchers observed dinoflagellate symbionts moving long-range within acoel worm hosts via host actin machinery. The symbionts traveled at ~1 μm/s within ultra-thin host parenchymal cells, with mobility regulated by diel rhythms and regeneration. The findings reveal a host-driven mechanism for maintaining symbiont distribution in dynamic homeostasis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dinoflagellate symbionts move long-range within aco:el worm hosts at ~1 μm/s",
    "Mobility is driven by host actin machinery despite confinement in ultra-thin parenchymal cells",
    "Symbiont distribution is spatiotemporally regulated by diel rhythms and regeneration"
  ],
  "study_type": "Long-term tracking, fluorescence, and electron microscopy",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a host-cytoskeleton-driven mechanism for active symbiont transport, expanding understanding of how holobionts maintain dynamic homeostasis through host-directed mobility."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates Re-functionalized Ti-MOFs for solar energy storage, demonstrating their ability to harvest, store, and release photogenerated charge under visible light. The researchers synthesized COK47-bpy and ReCl47-bpy, showing Re incorporation enhances charge retention, enables visible-light response, and allows on-demand hydrogen evolution with >90% efficiency. The materials achieve 19.5 C g-1 storage in colloids and 7.0 mAh g-1 in photoelectrodes, highlighting their potential for solar-driven energy storage systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Re-functionalized Ti-MOFs (ReCl47-bpy) achieve 19.5 C g-1 electron storage capacity in colloidal suspension under solar irradiation",
    "The material retains 70% of stored charge after 2.5 months and enables >90% electron-to-hydrogen evolution efficiency",
    "FTO-supported ReCl47-bpy photoelectrodes deliver up to 7.0 mAh g-1 capacity under 1 Sun irradiation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Synthetic photochargeable materials",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes Re-functionalized Ti-MOFs as versatile platforms for solar-driven charge storage and dark photocatalysis, advancing the development of MOF-based energy devices for continuous solar energy utilization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of achieving on-demand nanomotor retention at target sites by developing a PNA-triggered engine-disassembly braking mechanism. The approach uses programmable PNA to anchor catalytic engines to nanomotors, enabling competitive displacement upon PNA injection to halt motion. Results show enhanced tumor targeting and suppression after braking, demonstrating improved retention for sustained therapeutic effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PNA-triggered competitive displacement of catalytic engines halts nanomotor motion in vivo",
    "The braking mechanism enables precise tumor retention with superior therapeutic outcomes in mouse models",
    "Engine-disassembly strategy accommodates multiple catalytic functions for versatile applications"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo-controlled experimental study",
  "scientific_signingificance": "This work establishes a programmable braking mechanism for nanomotors, enabling targeted retention and sustained therapeutic effects without compromising deep tissue penetration capabilities."
  }

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether somatic CAG-repeat expansions in Huntington's disease neurons follow similar pathological pathways in cortical and striatal regions. Using molecular and pathological analyses, it found that both neuron types exhibit analogous sequence of pathological phases starting at ∼150 CAGs, with distinct gene expression changes and 20-fold variation in expansion magnitude among cortical pyramidal neuron subtypes. Both regions develop nuclear inclusions of aggregated HTT protein beyond 150 CAGs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cortical pyramidal neurons undergo somatic CAG-repeat expansions starting at ∼150 CAGs, analogous to striatal neurons",
    "Expansion magnitude varies up to 20-fold among cortical pyramidal neuron subtypes",
    "Both cortical and striatal neurons form nuclear inclusions of aggregated HTT protein beyond 150 CAGs"
  ],
  "study_type": "Molecular and pathological analysis",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that somatic CAG-repeat expansions initiate comparable pathological sequences in distinct brain regions of Huntington's disease, revealing shared mechanisms of early neuronal degeneration despite regional differences in gene expression."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses unstable Zn metal interfaces in aqueous zinc-ion batteries by engineering a 'water-in-water' biphasic electrolyte with dextran droplets in a PEG-rich phase. The architecture buffers local Zn2+ accumulation, enabling stable cycling for 1100 hours at high current density and Ah-level pouch cells. The findings highlight interfacial electrostatics as the governing mechanism for Zn2+ transport.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A 'water-in-water' biphasic electrolyte with dextran droplets in PEG-rich phase buffers local Zn2+ accumulation",
    "Zn||Zn cells cycle stably for 1100 h at 10 mA cm-2 and 10 mAh cm-2",
    "Ah-level Zn||NaV3O8 pouch cells sustain long-term operation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Electrolyte engineering",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes interfacial electrostatics as the primary mechanism for regulating Zn2+ transport in aqueous zinc-ion batteries, overcoming traditional limitations of solvent chemistry."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether cytochalasin D (CytoD) could enhance extracellular vesicle (EV) production while maintaining therapeutic properties. Using monocytic and colorectal cancer cell lines, CytoD increased EV release by 8.27- to 10.06-fold, preserving EV size and surface charge. CytoD-EVs showed enrichment of MYH9 and adhesion proteins, with actomyosin-dependent contractility driving EV shedding. These EVs effectively delivered doxorubicin, demonstrating enhanced cytotoxicity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CytoD increased EV production by 8.27-fold in U937 cells and 10.06-fold in SW480 cells",
    "CytoD-EVs retained lineage-specific membrane proteins and enriched MYH9, adhesion proteins, and membrane trafficking regulators",
    "Actomyosin-dependent contractility via MYH9 was essential for CytoD-induced EV release, as inhibition or knockdown reduced EV production"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro cell culture",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cytochalasin D-induced cytoskeletal remodeling as a scalable method to enhance extracellular vesicle production while maintaining therapeutic functionality, providing a platform for improved drug delivery systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used multimodal spatial transcriptomics to investigate the relationship between somatic CAG repeat expansions, HTT inusing, and neuronal loss in Huntington's disease. By analyzing 428,173 cells in human cortical tissue, it identified layer 5-6 near-projecting neurons and L6b deep-layer excitatory neurons as selectively vulnerable, with >50% loss linked to large repeat expansions (>450 CAGs). Intranuclear inclusions were most common at intermediate expansions (250-350 CAGs) and correlated with broader transcriptional changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Layer 5-6 near-projecting neurons and L6b deep-layer excitatory neurons show >50% loss in HD cortex",
    "Somatic CAG expansions >450 CAGs correlate with selective neuronal loss in HD",
    "Intranuclear inclusions peak at intermediate CAG expansions (250-350 CAGs) and drive transcriptional changes"
  ],
  "study_type": "Multimodal spatial transcriptomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a framework for linking somatic CAG repeat expansions with protein pathology and neuronal vulnerability across cell types in Huntington's disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates oxygen vacancy engineering in high-entropy spinel oxides to achieve broadband infrared emission while maintaining structural stability. By vacuum annealing (MnCrFeNiCu)3O4 without altering cation composition, researchers enhanced emissivity from 0.668-0.726 to 0.932-0.902 across 0.78-16 µm. The approach preserves the spinel framework and demonstrates that oxygen vacancies can improve emission without compromising thermal stability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Vacuum annealing of (MnCrFeNiCu)3O4 increased infrared emissivity to 0.932-0.902 across 0.78-16 µm",
    "Oxygen vacancies created vacancy-derived states and redistributed charge without degrading the spinel framework",
    "The high-entropy spinel maintained structural integrity after 1000°C annealing for 5 hours"
  ],
  "study_type": "Vacuum annealing of high-entropy spinel oxide",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a method to engineer oxygen vacancies in multication spinels for broadband infrared emission while retaining high-temperature structural stability, providing a pathway to enhance thermal emission in advanced ceramics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a biodegradable shape-memory biliary stent coated with decellularized human amniotic membrane-curcumin hydrogel to address post-biliodigestive reconstruction stricture. In vivo assessments in rat and rabbit models showed reduced inflammation, fibrosis, and biliary obstruction compared to conventional stents, with evidence of gut microbiota modulation and bile acid pathway changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The PCT/BaSO4 stent core provided mechanical support and matched biliary healing timelines",
    "dHAM-Cur coating enhanced hydrophilicity and sustained curcumin release",
    "Functionalized stents reduced inflammatory infiltration and fibrosis while preserving biliary patency"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo animal models (rat subcutaneous, duodenal, and rabbit orthotopic bile duct)",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a biodegradable stent system that actively modulates the biliary microenvironment to promote healing, offering a potential therapeutic strategy for preventing post-reconstruction strictures without requiring secondary removal."
}

{
  "summary": "The study examines regulatory frameworks for plant breeding innovation, emphasizing the mismatch between safety assessments and current regulations that prioritize methods over product outcomes. It identifies constraints from regulatory approaches on innovations like immune receptor transfer and genome editing, advocating for science-based, product-focused evaluation to enable crop improvements without methodological bias.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Regulatory frameworks prioritize breeding methods over product safety in plant innovation",
    "Innovations such as immune receptor transfer and genome editing face regulatory constraints",
    "A shift toward product-focused regulation is necessary for effective crop improvement"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work underscores the need for regulatory systems to evaluate crop innovations based on their safety and efficacy rather than the technical methods used, advancing the principle of proportionate, science-driven regulation in agricultural biotechnology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a photocatalytic tandem system for direct urea synthesis from atmospheric CO2 and N2, overcoming the energy-intensive Bosch-Meiser process. The IL@MOF captures CO2 and reduces it to CO, while the HTP-Cu3-imi-COF couples CO with N2 into urea. The system achieves a urea production rate of 259.87 µg·gcat⁻¹·h⁻¹ under air, representing the first photocatalytic urea synthesis from atmospheric gases.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL@MOF captures atmospheric CO2 and photoreduces it to CO",
    "HTP-Cu3-imi-COF couples CO with ambient N2 into urea",
    "The tandem system achieves 259.87 µg·gcat⁻¹·h⁻¹ urea production rate under air"
  ],
  "study_type": "Photocatalytic tandem platform",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes the first photocatalytic urea synthesis from atmospheric CO2 and N2, demonstrating a modular cascade catalyst design that integrates capture and conversion for sustainable chemical production."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated a magnesium-loaded anisotropic hydrogel scaffold for tendon healing. The scaffold was designed to provide a regenerative microenvironment through immunomodulation and collagen remodeling. In vitro, it reduced TNF-α secretion, inhibited M1 macrophage polarization, and promoted tendon stem cell activity. In vivo, it increased M2 macro, IL-10, vascularization, collagen alignment, and mechanical strength, indicating enhanced tendon regeneration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Magnesium-loaded hydrogel reduced TNF-α secretion and inhibited M1 macrophage polarization in vitro",
    "The scaffold increased M2 macrophages and IL-10 expression while reducing tissue adhesion in vivo",
    "Enhanced tendon regeneration with improved collagen alignment, vascularization, and mechanical properties"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo experiments",
  "scientific_significance": "This biomimetic scaffold demonstrates a multifunctional approach to accelerate tendon healing by simultaneously modulating inflammation and promoting structural regeneration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether calorie restriction (CR) reduces DNA mutation rates and how mutation rate changes relate to lifespan extension. Using a model organism, the authors found CR decreases mutation accumulation but this reduction does not proportionally increase lifespan. The findings suggest CR's impact on aging mechanisms may be more complex than previously thought.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Calorie restriction reduces DNA mutation accumulation",
    "The mutation rate reduction does not scale with lifespan extension",
    "CR's effect on aging mechanisms may involve non-linear relationships"
  ],
  "study_type": "Model organism",
  "scientific_significance": "The study reveals that calorie restriction's benefit in extending lifespan does not directly correlate with its reduction in mutation rates, challenging assumptions about the relationship between mutation accumulation and aging."
}
